  "english": "5. Monday. Tone 6 [GK]. Fast of the Holy Cross. Canticle of the Fathers [Harst] Tone 3 [B1]: \"Blessed art thou, Lord God of our fathers\" (Or harts'n merots astuats).\n8. Thursday. Tone 1 [ADZ]. Fast. Feast of the Birth of the Holy Mother of God from Anna.\n11. Sunday. Tone 4 [BK]. Feast of the Exaltation of the Holy Cross. See until the tenth Sunday in the First Volume, keeping the order of this place.\n18. Sunday. Tone 3 [BZ]. Second [Sunday after the Cross]. Hymn of the Evening [Hambartsi] Tone 4 [BDZ]: \"At the grave\" (I gerezman) and \"They came to the grave\" (Yekin i gerezman). Barekendan [eve] of the Fast of the Cross of Varag.\n19. Monday. Tone 4 [BK]. Fast. Feast of Mamas and the others. Canticle of the Fathers [Harst] Tone 7 [DY]: \"Those who trust\" (Yusats'yalqn).\n21. Wednesday. Tone 6 [GK]. Canticle of the Fathers [Harst] of the Fast Tone 4 [BK]: \"The voice of the children\" (Mankants'n zdzayn).\n25. Sunday. Tone 2 [AK]. Third [Sunday after the Cross]. Feast of the Cross of Varag. The intervening period of eating meat [non-fasting period] is eight weeks.\n\nOctober\n2. Sunday. Tone 1 [ACH]. Fourth [Sunday after the Cross]. Hymn of the Evening [Hambartsi] Tone 1 [A3]: \"With the women\" (Ynd kanaysn).\n9. Sunday. Tone 8 [DK]. Fifth [Sunday after the Cross]. Hymn of the Evening [Hambartsi] Tone 8 [DK]: \"When they came\" (Yorzham yekin), and \"The angel descended\" (Ej hreshtakn), and \"The ranks of angels\" (Hreshtakats'n dasq).\n16. Sunday. Tone 7 [DZ]. Sixth [Sunday after the Cross]. Hymn of the Evening [Hambartsi] Tone 7 [DZ]: \"To the women\" (Kanants'n) and \"The awesome\" (Ahagin).\n23. Sunday. Tone 6 [GK]. Seventh [Sunday after the Cross]. Feast of the Discovery of the Cross.\n25. Tuesday. Tone 8 [DK]. Feast of the Saints of Hyperichus. Canticle of the Fathers [Harst] Tone 5 [G3]: \"Who the torments\" (Orq ztanjan s).\n26. Wednesday. Tone 1 [AZ]. Canticle of the Fathers [Harst] of the Fast Tone 7 [DZ]: \"Blessed art thou, Lord God\" (Orhneal es ter astuats). \"Who the wondrous\" (Or zhrashali).\n30. Sunday. Tone 5 [GZ]. Eighth [Sunday after the Cross]. Hymn of the Evening [Hambartsi] Tone 5 [G3]: \"By the wood of the sign of the cross\" (I khachanish payten).\n\nNovember\n6. Sunday. Tone 4 [BK]. Ninth [Sunday after the Cross]. Hymn of the Evening [Hambartsi] Tone 4 [BK]: \"Christ is risen\" (ZKristos yareaw) and \"Morning\" (Arawot).\n13. Sunday. Tone 3 [BDZ]. Tenth [Sunday after the Cross]. Hymn of the Evening [Hambartsi] Tone 3 [B3]: \"The same messenger\" (Zoyn awetawor), to the end.\n14. Monday. Tone 4 [BK]. Feast of Andrew the Commander and his army, etc.\n15. Tuesday. Tone 5 [GZ]. Feast of Adrianus and his wife Anatolia, etc. Canticle of the Fathers [Harst] Tone 2 [AK]: \"Who art exalted\" (Or bardzreall).\n17. Thursday. Tone 7 [DZD]. Feast of Abraham and Khoren, of Cosmas and Damian, and of Astuatsatur the Martyr. Canticle of the Fathers [Harst] Tone 3 [B3]: \"Bearing no malice\" (Anokhakar).\n19. Saturday. Tone 1 [ACHZ]. All Saints, old and new, known and unknown.\n20. Sunday. Tone 2 [AK]. Eleventh [Sunday after the Cross]. Canticle of the Fathers [Harst] Tone 1 [AD]: \"Blessed art thou, Lord\" (Orhneal es ter). Hymn of the Evening [Hambartsi] Tone 2 [AK]: \"He is risen\" (Yaruts'eal) and \"Wondrous\" (Sqanch'eli). Barekendan [eve] of the Fast of the Fifty Days [Advent].\n21. Monday. Tone 3 [BDZ]. Fast. Feast of the Presentation of the Holy Mother of God.\n22. Tuesday. Tone 4 [BK]. Fast. Canticle of the Fathers [Harst] Tone 7 [DZ]: \"God of our fathers, who didst deliver\" (Harts'n merots astuats or apreguts'er).\n27. Sunday. Tone 1 [AZ]. First [Sunday of Advent]. Canticle of the Fathers [Harst] Tone 2 [AK]: \"Who for our salvation\" (Or vasn meroy prkut'ean). Hymn of the Evening [Hambartsi] Tone 1 [OY]: \"Ineffable by essence\" (Or anchar eut'eamb).\n28. Monday. Tone 2 [AK]. Feast of Julian and Vasilouhi. Canticle of the Fathers [Harst] Tone 3 [B]: \"With thy saints\" (Ynd surbs qo).\nAnd the rest according to the order in the First Volume, keeping the order of this place.\n\nDecember\n4. Sunday. Tone 8 [DK]. Second [Sunday of Advent]. Canticle of the Fathers [Harst] Tone 3 [B]: \"Incorruptible\" (Anapakan). Hymn of the Evening [Hambartsi] Tone 8 [DK]: \"Thine angel\" (Hreshtak qo).\n5. Monday. Tone 1 [AZ]. Feast of Genarius and Mercurius, and of Jacob and Iravap'ar.\n6. Tuesday. Tone 2 [AK]. Feast of King Abgar. The Scripture reading and Gospel are those of Theodosius.\n9. Friday. Tone 5 [GDZ]. Feast of the Conception of the Holy Virgin by Anna.\n11. Sunday. Tone 7 [DZ]. Third [Sunday of Advent]. Canticle of the Fathers [Harst] Tone 4 [BK]: \"Unoriginate God\" (Anskizbn astuats). Hymn of the Evening [Hambartsi] Tone 5 [G3]: \"Who art above\" (Or i verd es). Barekendan [eve] of the Fast of Saint James.\n14. Wednesday. Tone 2 [SK]. Canticle of the Fathers [Harst] Tone 7 [DZ]: \"Lord our God who didst establish\" (Ter astuats mer or hastatets'er).\n18. Sunday. Tone 6 [GK]. Fourth [Sunday of Advent]. Canticle of the Fathers [Harst] Tone 5 [G3]: \"Glorified Son\" (Paraworeal ordi). Hymn of the Evening [Hambartsi] Tone 6 [GK]: \"The divine\" (Zastuatsayin), and \"Thy resurrection\" (Zqo yarut'iund), and \"Taking also us\" (Areal ev mer).\n24. Saturday. Tone 4 [BK]. Feast of David the Prophet and James the Apostle.\n25. Sunday. Tone 5 [GD]. Fifth [Sunday of Advent]. Canticle of the Fathers [Harst] Tone 6 [GK]: \"Before eternity\" (Nakhayawitean). Hymn of the Evening [Hambartsi] Tone 5 [G3]: \"Glorified is thy resurrection\" (Paraworeal e qo yarut'iund), to the end.",
